                  // Copy is the three emails written in
                  // docs/alex-bristor.md, kept close to verbatim — hence
                  // three touches, all email, where the two sequences
                  // below run five across three channels. The doc has no
                  // LinkedIn or call touch and inventing one would be
                  // writing outreach the author didn't.
                  //
                  // The evidence layer around that copy — popover titles,
                  // questions and bodies, source labels, the Email
                  // Type / Reasoning pairs and the alternates — is drafted
                  // here to match the two sequences below, since the doc
                  // carries none of it. Every popover body states a fact
                  // from the doc's Account Context (8+ GTM tools, 290+
                  // SDRs, the DACH founding BDR team, the Dark TAM
                  // Engine); only the generic benchmarks are house
                  // boilerplate, same as in Natalie's and Max's.
                  //
                  // The doc's copy says "cross-sell SDRs" while this
                  // account's story is the enterprise/DACH motion. Rather
                  // than rewrite the author's line, each alternate below
